WEBVTT

00:00:00.213 --> 00:00:04.736
Open Unregister PE from PC under Workflows, or its matching Scripts

00:00:04.736 --> 00:00:08.909
action. Enter the PC endpoint, saved PC credential reference

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.448
and exact PE cluster UUID.

00:00:11.648 --> 00:00:14.875
Generating YAML does not contact a target.

00:00:15.046 --> 00:00:19.560
This administrator-only action has its own guarded job path and is not a general

00:00:19.611 --> 00:00:21.552
pipeline or scheduled step.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.296
Use Look up target, read-only.

00:00:24.518 --> 00:00:28.904
This requires strict certificate verification and supported PC APIs;

00:00:28.955 --> 00:00:33.651
it has no TLS bypass. Review the expected PC UUID

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.891
and PE name from inventory.

00:00:36.091 --> 00:00:40.265
Missing, ambiguous or mismatched identities block removal instead

00:00:40.315 --> 00:00:41.735
of choosing a similar cluster.

00:00:41.995 --> 00:00:46.219
Check the version-specific unregistration procedure and dependencies such as

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:50.478
replication, networking, application management and self-service

00:00:50.528 --> 00:00:54.416
configuration. The lookup does not certify those relationships.

00:00:54.564 --> 00:00:58.780
Record the dependency acknowledgement and have another administrator approve
the exact

00:00:58.831 --> 00:01:03.546
YAML and filename. Only after validation and exact confirmation

00:01:03.725 --> 00:01:07.898
does the worker recheck identities, require the vendor dry-run task

00:01:07.949 --> 00:01:11.013
to succeed and submit one unregister request.

00:01:11.191 --> 00:01:15.223
An uncertain submission or cancellation can leave remote work running.

00:01:15.387 --> 00:01:19.703
Inspect and reconcile PC state before requesting a further attempt.

00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:24.566
Review the PC task and inventory result against the original UUID.

00:01:24.758 --> 00:01:29.025
PC-side success does not establish that every PE-side cleanup

00:01:29.025 --> 00:01:31.128
or application dependency is complete.

00:01:31.329 --> 00:01:36.014
Follow the documented PE cleanup handoff and site acceptance procedure.

00:01:36.235 --> 00:01:39.274
Keep the original job and approval as the audit record.
